    <node id="Halcyon Retail Group">
      <data key="d0">Halcyon Retail Group</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Halcyon Retail Group is an organization involved in financial transactions, particularly in the context of invoicing and payment processing. It is identified as the payer in the 1099-NEC form, providing payment details for nonemployee compensation. The entity is also noted as the organization billed for services, with a consistent address listed as 1200 Commerce Blvd, Columbus, OH 43215. This address appears to be a fixed location, suggesting a centralized billing or administrative hub for the entity. Halcyon Retail Group is further described as a client organization billed for invoices, including specific invoice numbers such as DAVID-HALCYON-005 and PRIYA-HALCYON-001. The organization is consistently associated with receiving invoices, indicating its role as a recipient of financial obligations related to services rendered.

The entity has been billed for services rendered by Priya Raman and received an invoice with the number PRIYA-HALCYON-005. Additionally, Halcyon Retail Group is noted as a company that received a payment of $1,650.00 from David Okafor's account. It is also described as a company that made a payment to David Okafor's account, specifically a payment of $1,650.00 on 2025-03-02. These descriptions collectively highlight the dual role of Halcyon Retail Group as both a recipient and a payer in financial transactions, underscoring its involvement in various service-related financial obligations.

Halcyon Retail Group is also described as a merchant or business entity that made payments to or from the accounts of individuals such as Priya Raman and David Okafor. For instance, it is noted as a merchant that made a payment of $3,200.00 on January 2, 2025, from Priya Raman's account, and as a merchant that processed a payment of $3,200.00 from Priya Raman's account. Additionally, it is described as a merchant that made a payment to Priya Raman's account on 2025-04-02, and as a merchant that made a payment of $3,200.00 to Priya Raman's account on 2025-05-02. These descriptions suggest that Halcyon Retail Group is actively engaged in financial interactions with multiple parties, both as a recipient and a payer.&lt;SEP&gt;A merchant or business entity that made a payment to Priya Raman's account.</data>
